<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the MAIN APP (Contents/MacOS/Cookrew) may do under the hardened runtime.
  Everything else in the bundle gets entitlements.mac.inherit.plist.

  Deliberately left out, though electron-builder's default template has the
  first two:

  cs.disable-library-validation
    Only needed to load code signed by someone else. Electron's frameworks and
    node-pty's pty.node are all signed with this app's Team ID at build time, so
    library validation passes, and leaving it on is what stops a planted dylib.
    The binaries Cookrew runs (herdr, tmux, node, agents) are child processes,
    which library validation does not touch.

  cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    V8 asks for MAP_JIT memory, which allow-jit covers. Nothing here uses
    executable memory without it.

  cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
    Nothing here injects a dylib. The stripping applies to this process, not to
    what a pane's shell later exports for its own children.

  automation.apple-events
    Cookrew sends none: mac-bridge.ts drives input through CoreGraphics from
    JXA, on purpose, so it needs no Automation grant.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- V8 generates machine code at runtime in the main process, so without this the app dies at launch. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- Microphone. cr-listen is a child of this app, and macOS attributes a child's microphone use to the app that started it, so the grant has to be requestable here. Hardened apps without this are refused with no dialog. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- Camera, for cam:// cards. capture-host.ts calls systemPreferences.askForMediaAccess('camera'), which a hardened app without this answers false with no dialog. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
